From: CB1 <cb1@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nvkms: qualify exact native LLDV RGB and 444 transports

Reuse the integer primary and native output formatter for RGB and YCbCr444
at 10/12 bits, and for native YCbCr422 at 10 bits. Keep both RGB8 carriers.
Advertise the intersection of native HDMI/GPU, deep-color, Dolby EDID and
297 MHz CTA transport capabilities. Require exact format, depth and range;
never silently downgrade a selected native transport. Report the accepted
native enum, so a failed transition cannot confirm a different old format.
Preserve the no-LUT integer path and perform color encoding once in OCSC1.

